From aecf3818d5a8756bf7ef825fd659894fa210df3d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 17:45:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): release idle green PR owners and bound
 publication holds [daveey]

The active_pr duplicate-publication guard discharged terminal PRs and explicit
handoffs, but never discharged a bound open PR merely because its checks finished
green. Its generic six-hour hold cap exceeded the two-hour fairness threshold.
A diagnostic reporting zero failing checks was not a release or a wake source.

Reuse exact-head required CI acceptance, fail closed for missing evidence, and
admit only an idle ready publisher when every unfinished holding PR is green,
including local-only multi-publication cards like the original incident.
Preserve open-run and wake-probe custody. Collect in a two-worker
background pool with no backlog; guard ticks never wait for acceptance. Scope
cached observations to DB, task, publisher run, comment watermark and head;
discard observations taking over 120s, refresh after 300s, bound cache at 256.
Revalidate custody/publication identity before admission. This permits finishing
the existing PR, never bypasses exact-head independent review or merge gates;
ordinary crash/spend breakers still apply to subsequent recovery attempts.

Cap remaining active_pr holds at 2100s (35 min) using the existing home-owned
supervisor escalation. Preserve the existing 30-min notice and every existing
guard test unedited. Other guards keep their configured caps/exemptions.

Proof: fail-first idle-green returns active_pr; base cap is 21600 not 2100.
Pre-background compatibility selection: 50 files,1116 pass,0 fail,1 existing skip.
New custody/async tests exercise real dispatch, blocked network, two-job bound,
late observations, head/contract/assignee/watch/publication races and TTL.

